# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SWAG admin panel — environment. Copy to `.env.local` for local dev and set the
# same keys in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables for prod.
# NOTHING in here is safe to commit. All values are read server-side only
# (route handlers). None are prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, so none reach the browser.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Expo Push (Task 7) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Only required if you enabled "Enhanced Security for Push
# Notifications" in the Expo project. When set, it is sent as a Bearer token to
# the Expo push service. Leave blank to send unauthenticated (works by default).
EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Admin auth gate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret protecting the MUTATING routes (send push, edit version-config,
# delete token). If unset, those routes are OPEN — fine for local dev, but SET
# THIS IN PRODUCTION. The UI prompts for it and sends it as `x-admin-token`.
# The public /api/register and GET /api/version-config are intentionally unguarded
# (the app calls them without a secret).
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# ── Persistent storage (Bonus: token registry + durable version-config) ─────
# Provide EITHER of the following pairs. If neither is set, the app falls back to
# an in-memory store that is per-instance and resets on cold start (fine for a
# quick demo, NOT durable — see ARCHITECTURE.md "Storage" edge cases).
#
# Option A — Upstash Redis (create a free DB at https://upstash.com):
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Option B — Vercel KV / Marketplace (auto-injected when you attach a KV store):
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
